From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:38:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: implement CompositionEffectFactory and
 CompositionEffectBrush

CreateEffectFactory and CreateEffectFactoryWithProperties were stubs, and
PowerPoint's Presentation.Close depends on them: its cross fade is an
IGraphicsEffect that IGraphicsEffectD2D1Interop describes as an
ArithmeticComposite with two parameter sources and two animatable amounts
(Crossfade.Source1Amount and Source2Amount, the Y and Z of the coefficients).

The factory takes the whole graph when it is made: each effect's CLSID, the
property values it gives, and its sources, parameters by name or other
effects.  The names it is given to animate are looked up through
GetNamedPropertyMapping; a name no effect or property answers to is refused.
LoadStatus is Success.

The brush holds the brushes it draws from by parameter name, and the animatable
properties as values of its own, which it may be given in its property set and
animated like any property.  A property name with a dot is now a property of
that whole name when the object has one, as Effect.Property is; otherwise the
last or first dot separates a member, as in Offset.X.

On Windows the compositor draws effect brushes.  Here the compositor draws with
Direct2D, which now draws effect graphs, so the brush makes the graph's
Direct2D effects on the target's context, sets what may be animated as it is
now, and draws each source brush into a bitmap the size of the visual first,
on a context of its own so the target's clips stay as they are.  Opacity is an
ArithmeticComposite with the output as both inputs.

composition: 571 tests, 0 failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9774404b993721b732f916ec30932301f94bcd03)

